From e09de762e448ebaf3c136694538821747f3eec6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Braga?= <code@andrebraga.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: report a scan cut short by a firmware crash as
 aborted

When the firmware crashes during a scan, recovery halts the radio and
finishes the scan through ath12k_core_halt(). A scan in the RUNNING
state is then reported to mac80211 as completed, not aborted, although
the firmware never finished it and is gone.

Userspace takes the partial results as final and acts on them at once:
on a WCN7860 iwd tried to connect to two BSSes from a cut-off scan, and
both attempts failed with -ESHUTDOWN before the hardware restart was
requested, about a second later.

Mark a running scan as aborting before finishing it from the halt path,
so the completion carries aborted = true and userspace rescans after
the restart.

Tested-on: WCN7860 hw2.0 PCI WLAN.GNG.1.0-04065-QCAGNGSWPL_V1.0_V2.0_SILICONZ-1
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
index 6e04d1e6b..aad5ec970 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -1461,7 +1461,12 @@ void ath12k_core_halt(struct ath12k *ar)
 	ar->num_created_vdevs = 0;
 	ar->allocated_vdev_map = 0;
 
-	ath12k_mac_scan_finish(ar);
+	/* The firmware is gone, so a scan it was running never completed. */
+	spin_lock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
+	if (ar->scan.state == ATH12K_SCAN_RUNNING)
+		ar->scan.state = ATH12K_SCAN_ABORTING;
+	__ath12k_mac_scan_finish(ar);
+	spin_unlock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
 	ath12k_mac_peer_cleanup_all(ar);
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&ar->scan.timeout);
 	cancel_work_sync(&ar->regd_update_work);
-- 
